**2.2 Key Genomic Findings for Disease Net Construction**

**AR pathway alterations:** Present in 40--60% of mCRPC (AR
amplification, mutations, splice variants including AR-V7). These define
the sensitive population\'s vulnerability.

**DNA repair deficiency:** BRCA2 (12%), ATM (5%), BRCA1 (1.5%) --- total
HRR deficiency \~19.3%. These define the olaparib/talazoparib-sensitive
resistant population.

**TP53/RB1 co-loss:** Associated with treatment resistance,
neuroendocrine differentiation, and worst outcomes. RB1 alteration is
the strongest predictor of poor survival.

**PTEN loss:** \~40% of mCRPC. Activates PI3K pathway as escape route
when AR is blocked.

**3. Transcriptomic Layer: Gene Expression & Single-Cell**

The transcriptomic layer is where INTERCEPTA\'s unique contributions
live: KAALCURA axes require gene expression data, and RNA velocity
requires single-cell RNA-seq with unspliced/spliced read information.
This layer identifies cell populations and their trajectories.

