**4.2 Prostate-Specific Cell Lines in GDSC**

The following prostate cancer cell lines in GDSC are critical for
KAALCURA validation and ODE parameterization:

**LNCaP:** AR+, androgen-sensitive, PTEN-null. Models the sensitive
population. Expected high R_prolif.

**22Rv1:** AR+ with AR-V7 splice variant. Models castration-resistant
population.

**DU145:** AR-negative, mesenchymal features. Models EMT-transitioned
resistant population. Expected high R_emt.

**PC-3:** AR-negative, neuroendocrine features. Models NEPC lineage.

**VCaP:** AR amplified, TMPRSS2-ERG fusion. High AR dependency.

**C4-2B:** LNCaP-derived CRPC subline. Bone metastasis model.

**5. Pharmacokinetic/Pharmacodynamic Parameters**

The ODE simulation engine requires real PK/PD parameters for every drug
in the 15-drug mCRPC library. These come from published Phase I/II
pharmacokinetic studies and FDA drug labels.

**5.1 Critical Drug PK Parameters**

  -------------- ---------- ---------- ---------- --------------- ----------- ----------------
  **Drug**       **Dose**   **Cmax**   **t1/2**   **Bioavail.**   **Protein   **Source**
                                                                  Bind.**     

  Docetaxel      75 mg/m²   3.7 μg/mL  11.1 hr    IV (100%)       94-97%      FDA label;
                 IV                                                           Clarke 1999

  Abiraterone    1000 mg PO 226 ng/mL  12 hr      \~10%           \>99%       FDA label; Chi
                                                                              2015

  Enzalutamide   160 mg PO  16.6 μg/mL 5.8 days   \~84%           97-98%      FDA label;
                                                                              Gibbons 2015

  Olaparib       300 mg BID 7.9 μg/mL  11.9 hr    \~42%           82%         FDA label;
                 PO                                                           McCormick 2018

  Talazoparib    0.5 mg PO  15.8 ng/mL 90 hr      \~69%           74%         FDA label; Yu
                                                                              2020

  Prednisone     5 mg PO    \~25 ng/mL 3.5 hr     \~70%           65-91%      FDA label;
                                                                              standard refs
  -------------- ---------- ---------- ---------- --------------- ----------- ----------------

These parameters feed directly into the PK/PD module of our ODE engine.
Drug concentration over time is modeled as a one- or two-compartment
pharmacokinetic model, then coupled to the tumor dynamics equations
through Hill-equation dose-response functions. Each drug\'s effect on
the sensitive and resistant populations is parameterized independently
using KAALCURA-predicted sensitivity per population.

**6. Pathway & Network Layer**

The pathway layer builds the connections between net nodes. Mutations
and expression changes mean nothing in isolation --- they must be placed
in the context of signaling pathways to identify escape routes and
vulnerabilities.

